isaacsim must to turned on first
./isaac-sim.sh

adding virtul camera to isaaclab:
Load the SO-101 robot USD
Select the wrist link
Add → Sensor → Camera

config file for virtual arm:
nano configs/so101_wrist_cam.yaml
observations:
  wrist_rgb:
    type: camera
    source: isaac
    camera_name: wrist_camera
    resolution: [640, 480]

actions:
  type: joint_position

robot:
  name: so101

code for running imitation learning:
python lerobot/scripts/collect.py \
  --env isaac \
  --config configs/so101_wrist_cam.yaml \
  --output datasets/so101_wrist_il \
  --episodes 50

~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~OTHER METHODS~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
add "camera" prim
from omni.isaac.sensor import Camera
wrist_cam = Camera(
    prim_path="/World/Robot/wrist_link/WristCamera",
    resolution=(640, 480),
    frequency=30,
)
wrist_cam.initialize()

different example of config path:
cameras:
  wrist:
    type: isaac_sim
    prim_path: /World/Robot/wrist_link/WristCamera
    width: 640
    height: 480

FIXING THE CAMERA FOCUS:
the camera itself has a screw lens which is manually turned to change the focus. it cannot be automatically adjusted using the code
